Python codes to simulate stochastic wave equations, namely Saint-Venant, Boussinesq and Serre-Green-Naghdi under the LU formalism.
The water waves equation is also implemented.

The file 'shallow_water_nonlinear_modifiedConservativeTrueCgrid.py' allows to do it.
Saint-Venant and Boussinesq are ok, Serre-Green-Naghdi is quite slow (should be optimized in the future).
The files 'computeMeanAndVariance.py' and 'makeStatsPlots.py' generate and plot the statistics of the aforementioned models (respectively).

The files 'water_waves_LU[...].py' deals with the water waves LU equations and its approximations.
The main model (water waves) runs but is very slow. Its approximations are faster, and are based on simplifications of the Dirichlet to Neumann operator.
